PostgreSQL migrations use the same Settings and infra/.env as the FastAPI app.
The application never creates tables or applies migrations during startup.

No revisions exist yet because no domain tables have been introduced.

From the repository root, after configuring the backend and starting PostgreSQL:

    backend/.venv/bin/alembic -c backend/alembic.ini current
    backend/.venv/bin/alembic -c backend/alembic.ini check

When adding the first domain model:

1. Extend backend.models.base.Base and import the model in backend/models/__init__.py
   so Alembic can discover its metadata.
2. Generate a revision from the repository root:

       backend/.venv/bin/alembic -c backend/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "add domain table"

3. Review both upgrade() and downgrade() before applying the revision:

       backend/.venv/bin/alembic -c backend/alembic.ini upgrade head

From the backend directory, use .venv/bin/alembic with the local alembic.ini.
Connection timeout uses DATABASE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS. Migration execution time is
not limited by the health check timeout.

Async migration pattern:
https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/cookbook.html#using-asyncio-with-alembic
